*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* ACCOUNT.PATH(account)
*
* The pathname of the account, from the accounts register: a null string if there is no such account.  The name may be in either
* case.
*
* A PATHNAME IS GIVEN ONLY WHERE THE ACCOUNT COULD OPEN IT, as !VOCPATH gives one: the program is internal so that it can ask the
* account's OS gate (K$PATH.OK) about the path, which is always yes for the account's own directory and, for another account's,
* yes only when the caller's account has the OS access gate.  Without it the answer for another account is a null string, the
* same as for an account that does not exist, so that a program cannot find out which accounts there are, or where, by asking.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function accountpath(account)
$catalog !accountpath

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h

   path = ''
   name = downcase(trim(account))
   if name # '' then
      openpath @sdsys:@ds:'accounts' to acc.f then
         read acc.rec from acc.f, name then path = parse.pathname.tokens(acc.rec<ACC$PATH>)
         close acc.f
      end
   end

   * 18 Oct 26 Windows port - Linux asks the kernel's path test, the S.63 OS-access gate, which is held here (no such key).  What
   * stands in for it is the rule an account WITHOUT the gate gets on Linux: the path of the session's own account is told, and any
   * other only to an administrator session (SDSYS), which can read it anyway.  The deviation is told to Linux.
   * The register holds a drive letter path ("C:/ProgramData/SD/user_accounts/don"); @PATH, FILEINFO(FL$PATH) and VOCPATH() give the
   * same directory in this process's own spelling ("/cygdrive/c/ProgramData/..."), which is also what a program can open.  Both
   * are brought to that spelling, so that the answer starts with a slash as on Linux and the own-account test compares like
   * with like (18 Oct 26: the first run found ACCOUNT.PATH of the caller's own account empty, because the two spellings never matched).
   if path # '' then
      path = convert(char(92), '/', path)
      if path[2, 1] = ':' then path = '/cygdrive/' : downcase(path[1, 1]) : path[3, 99999]
      ok = kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, -1)
      if not(ok) then
         own = convert(char(92), '/', @path)
         if own[2, 1] = ':' then own = '/cygdrive/' : downcase(own[1, 1]) : own[3, 99999]
         own = upcase(own) : '/'
         here = upcase(path) : '/'
         ok = (here[1, len(own)] = own)
      end
      if not(ok) then path = ''
   end
   return path
end

